---
interface Props {
  appliance: "washing-machine" | "dishwasher";
}

const { appliance } = Astro.props;
const isWasher = appliance === "washing-machine";
const headingId = `${appliance}-measurement-resource`;
const downloadPath = `/downloads/${appliance}-measurement-worksheet.pdf`;
const resourceName = isWasher ? "washing machine" : "dishwasher";
---

<section class="measurement-resource" aria-labelledby={headingId}>
  <h2 id={headingId}>Measure the opening and the space to use it</h2>
  <p>
    Keep three records: the finished opening, the dimensions of the exact model and the
    installation space its manufacturer requires. The overall width on a product page
    and the required cavity width describe different things; use the installation drawing
    to check which parts sit inside the opening.
  </p>
  <div class="measurement-diagrams">
    <figure>
      <img
        src={`/images/diagrams/${appliance}-opening.svg`}
        alt={`Front view of a ${resourceName}: A marks the finished opening width and B marks the height from the floor to the underside above.`}
        width="560"
        height="480"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>
        <strong>Measure the finished opening.</strong> Check at the front, middle and rear,
        and at more than one height. Record the smallest usable width and height,
        plus any trim, skirting or uneven surfaces. Measure cavity depth separately.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <img
        src={`/images/diagrams/${appliance}-working-depth.svg`}
        alt={isWasher
          ? "Top view of a front loader: C marks appliance body depth, D reaches the open door, and a separate area identifies the service route."
          : "Side view of a dishwasher: C marks body depth, D reaches the lowered door, and a separate line identifies the service route."}
        width="560"
        height="480"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>
        <strong>Check the full working space.</strong> Follow the manual's definition of body,
        closed-door and open-door depth. Check hoses and connections separately, then leave
        room {isWasher ? "for the person loading the machine. For a top loader, check the fully raised lid as well."
          : "to extend the lower rack and stand in front. For a drawer dishwasher, check full drawer extension instead."}
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <p class="diagram-note">Original Australian Home Collective diagrams. Illustrative only, not to scale; the shaded areas do not specify a clearance.</p>
  <div class="measurement-download">
    <div>
      <h3>Take the measurements with you</h3>
      <p>Use the free one-page A4 worksheet to record the opening, exact model, installation requirements and delivery checks. Leave unknown measurements blank until confirmed.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="button" href={downloadPath} download data-measurement-download={appliance}>
      Download {resourceName} worksheet (PDF)
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .measurement-resource { margin: 2.5rem 0; }
  .measurement-diagrams { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.35rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 0.8rem; }
  figure { margin: 0; min-width: 0; }
  figure img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border: 1px solid #d5e1dc; border-radius: 12px; }
  figcaption { margin-top: 0.85rem; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.65; color: #263b3e; }
  figcaption strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
  .measurement-resource .diagram-note { font-size: 0.85rem; color: #4c625b; line-height: 1.5; }
  .measurement-download { margin-top: 1.5rem; padding: 1.4rem; background: #f0f5f2; border: 1px solid #d5e1dc; border-radius: 14px; }
  .measurement-download h3 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .measurement-download p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .measurement-download .button { max-width: 100%; white-space: normal; text-align: center; line-height: 1.5; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .measurement-diagrams { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.6rem; } .measurement-download { padding: 1.1rem; } }
  @media print { .measurement-resource { break-inside: auto; } figure { break-inside: avoid; } .measurement-download { background: white; } }
</style>
